    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Digital Realty Trust, Inc., which also goes by Digital Realty, is a for-profit public company headquartered in Austin, Texas, and traded under the ticker DLR. Its own site presents it as a data center, colocation, and interconnection provider, offering capacity across a global ecosystem that includes data centers, connectivity, and cloud services. The company describes its platform as the world's largest, spanning single racks, private suites, and high-density AI workflows, and says it is built for flexibility, open ecosystems, and reach.\n\nOn AI, the site frames infrastructure as the bottleneck rather than the software. It states that inference loads and GPU demands are pushing traditional environments to their limits, and that AI is evolving faster than infrastructure can follow. It also points to a 2026 Global Data Insights Survey, saying 40% of IT leaders cite infrastructure as an AI constraint and that enterprises are moving from AI strategy to execution.\n\nThe record for the company lists a litigation exposure count of 125 in Texas. It is registered with the SEC under CIK 0001297996.",
